1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Godot 4.7 editor with the Ziva panel on the left. A small sample game with one deliberate bug. Unedited, real time.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Prompt sent: add two more stars, make them spin, then play the game and check that the score goes up.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Ziva reads the scene tree and the project's scripts.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Ziva plans the change. The model is thinking; this pause is real time.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:34,500
Ziva edits star.gd (spin) and main.tscn (two new stars). The 2D view now shows five stars.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,500
Ziva runs the game and sends it the Right input action (ui_right). The player touches a star, but the score stays at 0.

7
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:47,000
The Debugger shows the runtime error: Node not found: "%ScoreLabel", then a null-instance error when the star is collected.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The first four Debugger lines are audio and display warnings from the virtual display this was recorded on.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:03,500
Ziva reads that error from the run and explains it: the label's unique name lives inside hud.tscn, not main.tscn.

10
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Ziva fixes the node path in main.gd to $HUD/ScoreLabel.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Ziva runs the game again, holding ui_right for 0.6 s. The score now reads 1.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Ziva reports what it changed and what it saw in the run screenshots.
